{# The model this thread runs on, rendered into the cached per-thread
   baseline: byte-deterministic for equal inputs, so no timestamps and no
   guidance fence. `content` is its label (`src/llms/model_identity.py`): the display
   name, and the reasoning effort when one was set. A switch between turns
   files a `model_changed` row rather than moving this block. A subagent
   cannot pick its model or run `la`, so it gets the fact alone. No model
   renders nothing. #}
{% if content %}
<model>
{% if subagent | default(false) %}
You run on {{ content }}.
{% else %}
You run on {{ content }}. The user picks the model; `la models list` shows the models they can run and who each one bills to.
{% endif %}
</model>
{% endif %}
